TEMPLATE NOTES (delete everything above the BEGIN:VCALENDAR line when
delivering — the delivered file must start at BEGIN:VCALENDAR):

Revision-calendar export for the pre-review-notes skill
(Step 3 of SKILL.md). Turns the chapter priority order into study
blocks the learner can import into any calendar app (Apple / Google /
Outlook / phone calendars all accept .ics).

Generation rules:
 - One VEVENT per study block. Number of blocks per chapter is
   proportional to its assessment weight (the 32/40-mark topic gets
   the most sessions), ending with a final quick-review pass over
   every chapter's quick-reference card in the last 1-2 days.
 - Work BACKWARD from the assessment date. The exam date and the
   learner's available days/hours must come from the learner or
   their materials — never guess or invent them.
 - Each DESCRIPTION says exactly what to do in that block (read
   chapter X notes / re-derive the worked problem from [source] /
   quick-reference pass), and cites the weight that justifies it.
 - Use floating local times (no trailing Z) unless the learner's
   timezone is known; for all-day blocks use DTSTART;VALUE=DATE.
 - Every UID must be unique. DTSTAMP is the generation time (UTC).
 - Output with CRLF line endings; fold lines longer than 75 octets
   (continuation lines start with a single space) per RFC 5545.

BEGIN:VCALENDAR
VERSION:2.0
PRODID:-//pre-review-notes//revision-plan//EN
CALSCALE:GREGORIAN
METHOD:PUBLISH
X-WR-CALNAME:[COURSE CODE] Revision Plan
X-WR-CALDESC:[One line: assessment date + weighting basis, e.g. "Final exam [date] - 32/40 marks computability, plan weighted accordingly"]
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:[course-code]-block-[n]@pre-review-notes
DTSTAMP:[YYYYMMDD]T[HHMMSS]Z
DTSTART:[YYYYMMDD]T[HHMMSS]
DTEND:[YYYYMMDD]T[HHMMSS]
SUMMARY:[COURSE CODE] · Ch.[X] [Topic] — block [n]/[total for this chapter]
DESCRIPTION:[What to do: e.g. work through Ch.[X] notes sections [X.1]-[X.3]\, then re-derive [real problem + source tag] without looking]\n权重依据 Weight basis: [e.g. 32/40 exam marks · recurs in every past sitting]
CATEGORIES:REVISION,[COURSE CODE]
BEGIN:VALARM
TRIGGER:-PT15M
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Revision block starting soon
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:[course-code]-final-pass@pre-review-notes
DTSTAMP:[YYYYMMDD]T[HHMMSS]Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:[YYYYMMDD]
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:[YYYYMMDD]
SUMMARY:[COURSE CODE] · Final pass — all quick-reference cards
DESCRIPTION:Last-minute review: read every chapter's quick-reference card and each "Must remember" box\, in priority order. Do not start new material.
CATEGORIES:REVISION,[COURSE CODE]
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
